# Obsidian keeps per-user state next to the shared settings. Which panes are open and
# where the cursor was are not facts about the project, and committing them means every
# person who opens the vault produces a diff.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache

# Community plugins are vendored third-party JavaScript and a per-person choice. The
# vault reads fine without any of them; `graph.json` and `app.json` are committed
# because those *are* shared decisions about how the vault looks.
.obsidian/plugins/
.obsidian/community-plugins.json
.obsidian/themes/

.trash/
